    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-8">Property Tax Returns & IRD Filing Requirements</h2>
    <p>Compliance is just as important as calculation. Landlords are legally obligated to declare their rental income on Property Tax Returns issued by the IRD. Individual owners typically report this on the Tax Return – Individuals (BIR60), while jointly owned properties are reported on a separate Property Tax Return (BIR57). Corporations use the Profits Tax Return (BIR51).</p>
    <p>Filing deadlines are strict. For individual tax returns, they are usually due within one month from the date of issue (typically early May). However, electronic filing via the <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-etax-guide/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">IRD eTAX Portal</a> is highly recommended, as it offers a seamless experience and automatically grants a 1-month filing extension. To survive an IRD audit, you must maintain meticulous records. Keep all tenancy agreements, bank statements, rent receipts, and correspondence regarding irrecoverable rent for at least 7 years.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary mt-8">Property Tax vs Stamp Duty: Understanding the Difference</h2>
    <p>A common point of confusion for new landlords is the difference between Property Tax and Stamp Duty. They are distinct obligations governed by different ordinances:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Property Tax:</strong> As discussed, this is an <em>annual</em> tax assessed on the ongoing rental income earned by property owners. It is managed by the IRD and filed yearly.</li>
      <li><strong>Stamp Duty:</strong> This is a <em>one-off</em> transaction tax. It is paid when executing documents such as tenancy agreements (often referred to as lease stamping) or when purchasing/transferring property (Ad Valorem Stamp Duty, Buyer's Stamp Duty, etc.). The cost of stamping a lease is typically shared equally between the landlord and the tenant. Learn more in our comprehensive <a href="/blogs/hong-kong-stamp-duty-guide/" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Hong Kong Stamp Duty Guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>

